course: dictionary
lesson: 9967
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning is right. «Mr Hughes walks in with a cup of tea.» You can have a cup of something, and you drink tea, so here tea is a hot drink.
explain: Tea can also mean an evening meal, especially for children, as in "What's for tea?" Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Tea can also mean the dried leaves themselves, or a drink made from other plants, such as mint tea. Each time, look at the words around it and choose the meaning that fits.
fact: Tea is a hot drink made by pouring boiling water onto dried leaves of the tea plant.
fact: "Tea" can also mean the dried leaves themselves.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, "tea" can mean an evening meal, especially for children.
fact: "Afternoon tea" is a light meal with cakes and sandwiches.
fact: Some drinks made from other plants are also called tea, like mint tea. Hot tea can burn small children, so keep hot drinks away from the edge of tables.
exercise: «Mr Hughes walks in with a cup of tea.» What is the tea here? | A meal eaten in the evening | A tree that grows in a garden | A type of biscuit | *A hot drink
exercise: Mia comes home from school and asks, "What's for tea?" What does tea mean here? | A hot drink made from leaves | A cake shop | *An evening meal | A kind of bus
exercise: Some drinks made from other plants are also called tea. Which one is a tea? | Mint toothpaste | Mint sauce | *Mint tea | A mint sweet
test: In «Thé ou café ?», the word ou means what in English? | tea | *or | coffee | where
test: Dad calls, "Tea's ready!" at six o'clock. What does tea mean here? | A cake with cream | A hot drink with milk, only at breakfast | *An evening meal | A bag of dried leaves
exam: «Sugar dissolves faster in hot tea.» What does this show? | *Sugar mixes into hot tea more quickly | Hot tea is always cold | Sugar sinks to the bottom and never mixes | Sugar is made from tea leaves
